# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site configuration — never committed.
#
# config.sh holds a site's values (paths, group and admin names, contact). config.example.sh is the committed template; copy it
# and fill it in. See README.md §Configure.
#
# Nothing in config.sh is a credential — see internal/CURRENT-STATE.md — but it
# is site topology, and keeping it out of the repo is what lets this tree be
# shared, forked or handed to a vendor without redaction.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
config.sh
config.*.sh
!config.example.sh

# Per-user Claude Code session state, not deployment config. .claude/skills/
# IS tracked - those are the maintenance skills, see .claude/README.md.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/.cc-writes/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Never commit a backup or a timestamped copy — they are how stale files come
# back to life after someone greps the tree and finds the wrong one first.
*.orig
*.orig.*
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.rej
*.tar.gz
